Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: contracting, and fuel subsidy programs which directly affect commuters and PUV drivers and operators.

asr-009674
09:00:10.260 --> 09:00:17.420
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: He likewise joined the call for the remittance of earmarked revenues intended for universal healthcare

asr-009675
09:00:17.420 --> 09:00:20.520
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: and adequate funding for field health.

asr-009676
09:00:21.760 --> 09:00:29.000
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Representative J.C. Abalos of 4Ps Partylist raised the implementation concerns

asr-009677
09:00:29.000 --> 09:00:32.700
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: regarding the community-based monitoring system.

asr-009678
09:00:32.700 --> 09:00:47.240
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: The proposed CBMS budget is about 5.062 billion, yet 4.92 billion, or 97%, is lodged in the Central Office,

asr-009679
09:00:47.700 --> 09:00:53.500
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: while 16 regions and BARMM share only 130 million.

asr-009680
09:00:53.500 --> 09:00:58.500
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: More importantly, 59,462 families.

asr-009681
09:00:59.000 --> 09:01:09.500
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: In the 4Ps set, 12 waitlists remain unmatched with CBMS data, some since 2023.

asr-009682
09:01:11.260 --> 09:01:20.020
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Representative Audrey Zubiri of the 3rd District of Bukidnon raised the continued funding shortfall

asr-009683
09:01:20.020 --> 09:01:23.300
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: under the Sugarcane Industry Development Act.

asr-009684
09:01:23.300 --> 09:01:28.240
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: The law provides for an aggregate of 2 billion annually.

asr-009685
09:01:29.000 --> 09:01:39.120
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Yet, approximately 1.020 billion was appropriated in the 2026 GA.

asr-009686
09:01:40.020 --> 09:01:42.640
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Her concern raises a broader principle.

asr-009687
09:01:42.640 --> 09:01:49.780
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: When Congress creates a program and provides a statutory funding mandate,

asr-009688
09:01:50.780 --> 09:01:55.420
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: annual budgets should give meaningful effect to that commitment.

asr-009689
09:01:56.460 --> 09:01:58.980
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Representative Presley De Jesus,

asr-009690
09:01:59.000 --> 09:02:01.260
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: of PHILRECA Partylist,

asr-009691
09:02:02.060 --> 09:02:06.740
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: called for stronger support for total missionary electrification,

asr-009692
09:02:07.420 --> 09:02:09.960
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: total and missionary electrification,

asr-009693
09:02:10.900 --> 09:02:13.760
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: noting that proposed budgetary support for NEA

asr-009694
09:02:13.760 --> 09:02:22.260
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: declines from 10.134 billion in 2026

asr-009695
09:02:22.260 --> 09:02:28.100
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: to 6.486 billion in 2027.

asr-009696
09:02:29.000 --> 09:02:35.760
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: While many electric cooperatives still need to expand service

asr-009697
09:02:35.760 --> 09:02:40.780
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: and rehabilitate aging distribution systems.

asr-009698
09:02:41.780 --> 09:02:49.020
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: He likewise raised the adequacy of the 2.001 billion allocation

asr-009699
09:02:49.020 --> 09:02:50.560
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: for missionary electrification,

asr-009700
09:02:51.700 --> 09:02:57.060
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: particularly as higher fuel costs affect national power corporation,

asr-009701
09:02:57.060 --> 09:02:58.060
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Small Power Utilities Group

asr-009702
09:02:59.000 --> 09:03:03.000
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: operations in off-grid communities.

asr-009703
09:03:03.000 --> 09:03:09.780
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: He also emphasized the need to strengthen ERC's regulatory capacity

asr-009704
09:03:09.780 --> 09:03:15.860
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: so that government addresses not only price spikes for temporary interventions,

asr-009705
09:03:15.860 --> 09:03:22.260
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: but their underlying causes, supply shortages, inadequate reserves,

asr-009706
09:03:22.900 --> 09:03:26.720
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: generation outages, and transmission congestion.

asr-009707
09:03:27.820 --> 09:03:28.780
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: The concern,

asr-009708
09:03:29.000 --> 09:03:34.000
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: the over-reliability and affordability was reinforced

asr-009709
09:03:34.000 --> 09:03:39.000
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: by Representative Sergio Dagooc of APEC Partylist,

asr-009710
09:03:39.000 --> 09:03:45.080
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: who focused particularly on the continuing energy problems in the Visayas.

asr-009711
09:03:45.820 --> 09:03:49.460
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: He emphasized that generation shortages,

asr-009712
09:03:50.220 --> 09:03:53.060
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: inadequate reserves and ancillary services,

asr-009713
09:03:53.820 --> 09:03:55.100
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: transmission congestion,

asr-009714
09:03:56.280 --> 09:03:57.700
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: and line rental charges

asr-009715
09:03:57.700 --> 09:03:59.000
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: must be addressed

asr-009716
09:03:59.000 --> 09:04:01.920
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: as one systemic problem.

asr-009717
09:04:02.880 --> 09:04:10.500
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: He likewise called for the rehabilitation of the Agus Pulangi hydro power complex

asr-009718
09:04:10.500 --> 09:04:14.240
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: while retaining government ownership and control,

asr-009719
09:04:14.820 --> 09:04:18.620
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: and a reassessment of a limited strategic role

asr-009720
09:04:18.620 --> 09:04:24.040
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: for NPC in emergency reserves and ancillary services,

asr-009721
09:04:24.040 --> 09:04:28.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: and consideration of a temporary,

asr-009722
09:04:29.000 --> 09:04:37.880
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: rule-based VAT shock absorber during extraordinary electricity and fuel price increases.

asr-009723
09:04:37.880 --> 09:04:45.560
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: His concern reminds us that energy policy is also economic policy.

asr-009724
09:04:46.560 --> 09:04:56.700
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: High power and fuel costs eventually find their way into transportation, food, production, and inflation.

asr-009725
09:04:56.700 --> 09:05:03.080
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Representative Bong Suntay of the 4th District of Quezon City emphasized

asr-009726
09:05:03.080 --> 09:05:07.800
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: that major appropriations must produce measurable results.

asr-009727
09:05:08.740 --> 09:05:15.040
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: He pointed to the P191.285 billion proposed

asr-009728
09:05:15.040 --> 09:05:20.500
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: for the Metro Manila Subway and North-South Commuter Railway,

asr-009729
09:05:20.500 --> 09:05:25.820
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: stressing that rail spending must ultimately be measured

asr-009730
09:05:25.820 --> 09:05:28.120
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: by working trains and improved mobility.

asr-009731
09:05:29.360 --> 09:05:31.700
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: He likewise called for health spending

asr-009732
09:05:31.700 --> 09:05:35.980
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: to reduce the still substantial out-of-pocket burden

asr-009733
09:05:35.980 --> 09:05:38.420
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: on Filipino families

asr-009734
09:05:38.420 --> 09:05:42.520
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: and for government to maintain a credible fiscal plan

asr-009735
09:05:42.520 --> 09:05:48.460
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: should revenues or economic growth fall below assumptions.

asr-009736
09:05:49.540 --> 09:05:53.060
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: These concerns differ in subject,

asr-009737
09:05:53.060 --> 09:05:55.060
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: but they reflect the same question before us:

asr-009738
09:05:55.820 --> 09:06:05.960
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: With limited resources, where can government spending make the greatest difference?

asr-009739
09:06:05.960 --> 09:06:12.960
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: That question applies equally to our investments in infrastructure.

asr-009740
09:06:12.960 --> 09:06:18.500
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Mr. Speaker, even with limited fiscal space,

asr-009741
09:06:18.500 --> 09:06:23.200
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: we should protect infrastructure that can expand the economy

asr-009742
09:06:23.200 --> 09:06:25.200
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: and improve national connectivity.

asr-009743
09:06:25.820 --> 09:06:32.340
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Our interpellation yesterday on the DPWH budget

asr-009744
09:06:32.340 --> 09:06:38.120
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: produced concrete commitments on the Sorsogon-Samar Link Bridge.

asr-009745
09:06:39.080 --> 09:06:43.380
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: We were informed that the government's 130 million

asr-009746
09:06:43.380 --> 09:06:48.020
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: for the feasibility study will be complemented

asr-009747
09:06:48.020 --> 09:06:51.380
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: by approximately 500 million from ADB,

asr-009748
09:06:51.380 --> 09:06:56.180
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: completing the estimated 650 million funding requirement.

asr-009756
09:06:57.320 --> 09:07:00.060
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Bidding is expected to begin this November

asr-009757
09:07:00.060 --> 09:07:05.720
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: with the study taking about one year.

asr-009758
09:07:07.320 --> 09:07:10.260
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Detailed engineering is targeted for 2028

asr-009759
09:07:10.260 --> 09:07:14.780
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: followed by civil works bidding in 2028 or early 2029.

asr-009760
09:07:15.620 --> 09:07:18.260
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: If the project proves feasible

asr-009761
09:07:18.260 --> 09:07:20.760
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: and the timetable is followed,

asr-009762
09:07:21.160 --> 09:07:24.280
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: completion could be around 2025

asr-009763
09:07:24.280 --> 09:07:26.300
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: or 2036.

asr-009764
09:07:26.920 --> 09:07:29.020
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: This is significant because

asr-009765
09:07:29.020 --> 09:07:31.300
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Secretary Vince Dixon cited an estimated

asr-009766
09:07:31.300 --> 09:07:35.240
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: 42% economic rate of return

asr-009767
09:07:35.240 --> 09:07:37.840
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: for the project and inform us

asr-009768
09:07:37.840 --> 09:07:39.200
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: of a strong interest

asr-009769
09:07:39.200 --> 09:07:43.880
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: from development partners and investors.

asr-009770
09:07:55.360 --> 09:07:59.300
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: This also should be a challenge to NEDA,

asr-009771
09:07:59.300 --> 09:08:03.300
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: DEPDev and DEPDev.

asr-009772
09:08:03.300 --> 09:08:08.300
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: ADB and higher development partners appear willing

asr-009773
09:08:08.300 --> 09:08:11.300
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: to support the mega projects

asr-009774
09:08:11.300 --> 09:08:13.300
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: when the economic case is strong.

asr-009775
09:08:13.300 --> 09:08:18.300
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Let us identify other major infrastructure projects

asr-009776
09:08:18.300 --> 09:08:21.300
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: with high economic rates of return,

asr-009777
09:08:21.300 --> 09:08:24.300
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: subject them to rigorous feasibility studies,

asr-009778
09:08:24.300 --> 09:08:25.300
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: and bring them to the table.

asr-009779
09:08:25.300 --> 09:08:27.300
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: If the project is a viable project to ADB,

asr-009780
09:08:27.300 --> 09:08:31.240
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: JICA, Korea, and other development partners,

asr-009781
09:08:31.240 --> 09:08:34.240
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Kung mataas ang economic return

asr-009782
09:08:34.240 --> 09:08:36.240
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: at may handang tumulong sa financing,

asr-009783
09:08:36.240 --> 09:08:39.240
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: hanapin natin ang mga proyektong ito

asr-009784
09:08:39.240 --> 09:08:41.240
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: at simulan natin.

asr-009785
09:08:41.240 --> 09:08:43.240
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: May pondo na,

asr-009786
09:08:43.240 --> 09:08:45.240
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: may timetable pa.

asr-009787
09:08:45.240 --> 09:08:47.240
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Ang mas mahalaga ngayon

asr-009788
09:08:47.240 --> 09:08:49.240
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: ay matupad ang mga commitment na ito.

asr-009789
09:08:49.240 --> 09:08:51.240
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: The vision, however,

asr-009790
09:08:51.240 --> 09:08:53.240
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: should extend beyond Sorsogon and Samar.

asr-009791
09:08:53.240 --> 09:08:55.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: For the

asr-009792
09:08:55.160 --> 09:08:58.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: for the Southern Leyte-Surigao Link,

asr-009793
09:08:58.160 --> 09:09:01.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: 350 million has been identified

asr-009794
09:09:01.160 --> 09:09:03.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: for the feasibility study

asr-009795
09:09:03.160 --> 09:09:08.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: with DPWH negotiating with ADB

asr-009796
09:09:08.160 --> 09:09:11.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: for additional funding required.

asr-009797
09:09:11.160 --> 09:09:14.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: During the same interpellation,

asr-009798
09:09:14.160 --> 09:09:17.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: we also obtained commitments

asr-009799
09:09:17.160 --> 09:09:21.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: to pursue funding for three additional inter-island links,

asr-009800
09:09:21.160 --> 09:09:24.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Maasin, Southern Leyte,

asr-009801
09:09:24.160 --> 09:09:26.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: to Lapinig Island,

asr-009802
09:09:26.160 --> 09:09:28.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: to Ubay, to Bohol,

asr-009803
09:09:28.160 --> 09:09:30.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Getafe, Bohol,

asr-009804
09:09:30.160 --> 09:09:32.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: to Cordoba, Cebu,

asr-009805
09:09:32.160 --> 09:09:35.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: and Santander, Cebu,

asr-009806
09:09:35.160 --> 09:09:37.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: to Sibulan, Negros.

asr-009807
09:09:37.160 --> 09:09:39.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: The DPWUH indicated

asr-009808
09:09:39.160 --> 09:09:42.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: that these projects could secure

asr-009809
09:09:42.160 --> 09:09:45.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: funding in the next budget

asr-009810
09:09:45.160 --> 09:09:48.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: and through development partners or investors

asr-009811
09:09:48.160 --> 09:09:51.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: with the Bohol-Cebu connection already studied

asr-009812
09:09:51.160 --> 09:09:53.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: by the department,

asr-009813
09:09:53.160 --> 09:09:57.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: and identified as a priority.

asr-009814
09:09:57.160 --> 09:09:59.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: We should also include

asr-009815
09:09:59.160 --> 09:10:05.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: the Camarines Sur-Catanduanes Inter-Island Connectivity Project

asr-009816
09:10:05.160 --> 09:10:08.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: or the Friendship Bridge

asr-009817
09:10:08.160 --> 09:10:12.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: being pushed by Representative Leo Rodriguez of Catanduanes,

asr-009818
09:10:12.160 --> 09:10:17.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: envisioned as a long-span bridge connecting Catanduanes

asr-009819
09:10:17.160 --> 09:10:19.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: to mainland Bicol.

asr-009820
09:10:19.160 --> 09:10:22.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: The project already has around 80 million

asr-009821
09:10:22.160 --> 09:10:25.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: in the 2026 GAA for feasibility study.

asr-009822
09:10:25.160 --> 09:10:28.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: It belongs to the same larger vision

asr-009823
09:10:28.160 --> 09:10:31.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: using strategic inter-island links

asr-009824
09:10:31.160 --> 09:10:34.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: to connect communities that geography

asr-009825
09:10:34.160 --> 09:10:36.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: has long kept apart.

asr-009826
09:10:37.160 --> 09:10:39.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Taken together,

asr-009827
09:10:39.160 --> 09:10:41.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: these proposed links

asr-009828
09:10:41.160 --> 09:10:43.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: could form part of a more integrated

asr-009829
09:10:43.160 --> 09:10:46.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: inter-island transport network

asr-009830
09:10:46.160 --> 09:10:48.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: across the Philippine archipelago,

asr-009831
09:10:48.160 --> 09:10:51.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: connecting Catanduanes to mainland Bicol,

asr-009832
09:10:52.160 --> 09:10:55.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Luzon to Samar, Samar to Leyte,

asr-009833
09:10:55.160 --> 09:10:57.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Leyte to Mindanao,

asr-009834
09:10:57.160 --> 09:11:00.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: while establishing additional fixed links

asr-009835
09:11:00.160 --> 09:11:02.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: from Leyte to Bohol,

asr-009836
09:11:02.160 --> 09:11:05.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Bohol to Cebu, Cebu to Negros,

asr-009837
09:11:05.160 --> 09:11:08.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: and eventually Negros to Panay,

asr-009838
09:11:08.160 --> 09:11:13.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: complementing the Panay-Guimaras-Negros Island Bridges project.

asr-009839
09:11:13.160 --> 09:11:16.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: In a period of slow economic growth,

asr-009840
09:11:16.160 --> 09:11:19.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: these are the kinds of transformative projects

asr-009841
09:11:19.160 --> 09:11:21.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: worth carefully pursuing.

asr-009842
09:11:21.160 --> 09:11:24.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Projects that can shorten travel time,

asr-009843
09:11:24.160 --> 09:11:26.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: lower logistics costs,

asr-009844
09:11:26.160 --> 09:11:28.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: open new markets,

asr-009845
09:11:28.160 --> 09:11:31.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: bring communities closer together,

asr-009846
09:11:31.160 --> 09:11:35.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: and ultimately expand the country's productive capacity.

asr-009847
09:11:35.160 --> 09:11:38.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: As this representation has said

asr-009848
09:11:38.160 --> 09:11:40.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: during the interpellation,

asr-009849
09:11:40.160 --> 09:11:45.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: we bring our people to their destination faster.

asr-009850
09:11:45.160 --> 09:11:49.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: We can bring our patients faster to our hospitals.

asr-009851
09:11:49.160 --> 09:11:50.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: We can move

asr-009852
09:11:50.160 --> 09:11:51.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: our goods faster,

asr-009853
09:11:51.160 --> 09:11:56.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: and we can bring our families closer together.

asr-009854
09:11:56.160 --> 09:12:00.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: But connectivity is not only an economic issue.

asr-009855
09:12:00.160 --> 09:12:03.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: In an archipelagic country,

asr-009856
09:12:03.160 --> 09:12:06.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: the same infrastructure that moves people and goods

asr-009857
09:12:06.160 --> 09:12:09.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: also strengthens our ability

asr-009858
09:12:09.160 --> 09:12:11.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: to respond to disasters,

asr-009859
09:12:11.160 --> 09:12:13.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: move resources,

asr-009860
09:12:13.160 --> 09:12:15.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: and secure our territory.

asr-009861
09:12:15.160 --> 09:12:17.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: This brings us to another concern

asr-009862
09:12:17.160 --> 09:12:19.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: raised during the budget deliberations

asr-009863
09:12:19.160 --> 09:12:24.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: the need to strengthen our eastern seaboard.

asr-009864
09:12:24.160 --> 09:12:27.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Our eastern coast is not only an economic corridor,

asr-009865
09:12:27.160 --> 09:12:30.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: it is also a strategic frontier.

asr-009866
09:12:30.160 --> 09:12:32.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: In recent weeks,

asr-009867
09:12:32.160 --> 09:12:35.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: the AFP confirmed monitoring foreign vessels

asr-009868
09:12:35.160 --> 09:12:38.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: passing off the coast of eastern Samar.

asr-009869
09:12:38.160 --> 09:12:41.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: The AFP assessed that particular passage

asr-009870
09:12:41.160 --> 09:12:45.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: as non-threatening and consistent with navigation

asr-009871
09:12:45.160 --> 09:12:47.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: through a normal shipping route.

asr-009872
09:12:47.160 --> 09:12:50.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: We accept that professional assessment,

asr-009873
09:12:50.160 --> 09:12:55.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: but it also reminds us of something basic.

asr-009874
09:12:55.160 --> 09:13:00.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Our defense posture cannot only be westward.

asr-009875
09:13:00.160 --> 09:13:04.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: The Philippines is an archipelago.

asr-009876
09:13:04.160 --> 09:13:09.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Our eastern approaches face Pacific

asr-009877
09:13:09.160 --> 09:13:12.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: and cover a vast maritime area.

asr-009878
09:13:12.160 --> 09:13:16.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: The AFP's comprehensive archipelagic defense concept itself

asr-009879
09:13:16.160 --> 09:13:21.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: recognizes the need to defend our entire maritime domain,

asr-009880
09:13:21.160 --> 09:13:24.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: including our exclusive economic zones

asr-009881
09:13:24.160 --> 09:13:26.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: and vital sea lanes.

asr-009882
09:13:26.160 --> 09:13:28.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Consequently,

asr-009883
09:13:28.160 --> 09:13:31.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Representative Christopher Sheen Gonzales

asr-009884
09:13:31.160 --> 09:13:34.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: of the Lone District of Eastern Samar proposes

asr-009885
09:13:34.160 --> 09:13:37.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: for the need to strengthen the country's defense posture

asr-009886
09:13:37.160 --> 09:13:39.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: along eastern seaboard.

asr-009887
09:13:39.160 --> 09:13:41.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: As our forces modernizes,

asr-009888
09:13:41.160 --> 09:13:44.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: he called for greater investments

asr-009889
09:13:44.160 --> 09:13:46.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: in maritime domain awareness,

asr-009890
09:13:46.160 --> 09:13:49.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: radar and surveillance,

asr-009891
09:13:49.160 --> 09:13:51.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: naval and air capacities,

asr-009892
09:13:51.160 --> 09:13:54.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: and strategic facilities

asr-009893
09:13:54.160 --> 09:13:56.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: along our Pacific coast

asr-009894
09:13:56.160 --> 09:13:58.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: that will enable our forces

asr-009895
09:13:58.160 --> 09:14:01.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: to effectively monitor and respond

asr-009896
09:14:01.160 --> 09:14:03.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: when necessary.

asr-009897
09:14:03.160 --> 09:14:07.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: This is not about identifying any country

asr-009898
09:14:07.160 --> 09:14:09.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: as an enemy.

asr-009899
09:14:09.160 --> 09:14:14.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: It is simply responsible national defense.

asr-009900
09:14:14.160 --> 09:14:16.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Kung pinapalakas

asr-009901
09:14:16.160 --> 09:14:19.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: natin ang depensa sa kaunlaran.

asr-009902
09:14:19.160 --> 09:14:22.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Hindi dapat pabayaan ang silangan.

asr-009903
09:14:22.160 --> 09:14:26.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Ang isang kapuluan ay dapat may kakayahang bantayan

asr-009904
09:14:26.160 --> 09:14:30.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: ang kanyang mga hangganan.

asr-009905
09:14:30.160 --> 09:14:32.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: The bridges and transport links

asr-009906
09:14:32.160 --> 09:14:35.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: we have discussed also have strategic dimension.

asr-009907
09:14:35.160 --> 09:14:41.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Better ports, roads, bridges, and logistics networks

asr-009908
09:14:41.160 --> 09:14:44.160
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: strengthen not only commerce

asr-009909
09:14:44.160 --> 09:14:50.580
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: but also disaster response, humanitarian assistance, and national resilience.

asr-009910
09:14:51.760 --> 09:14:58.680
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: A connected Eastern Seaboard should therefore be a part of a broader national strategy.

asr-009911
09:15:00.000 --> 09:15:13.520
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: We must protect it economically, secure it adequately, and ensure that development reaches the regions that have historically remained farthest from the centers of growth.

asr-009912
09:15:14.300 --> 09:15:20.960
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: And that brings us to another principle that should guide this budget – regional equity.

asr-009913
09:15:20.960 --> 09:15:35.780
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Earlier, House Policy Research found that budget shares of Visayas and Mindanao have historically fallen below the shares of the country's poor population.

asr-009914
09:15:36.600 --> 09:15:48.220
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Large appropriations classified as nationwide or central office expenditures also make geographic distribution difficult to determine at enactment.

asr-009915
09:15:48.220 --> 09:15:52.380
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: We are not asking for equal amounts for every region.

asr-009916
09:15:53.280 --> 09:16:05.580
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Allocations should reflect population, poverty, infrastructure, infrastructure gaps, disaster exposure, and geographic isolation.

asr-009917
09:16:06.640 --> 09:16:13.080
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Hindi dapat maging hadlang sa pag-unlad ang pagiging malayo sa sintro ng bansa.

asr-009918
09:16:13.700 --> 09:16:17.620
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: We acknowledge one important reform in this budget.

asr-009919
09:16:18.220 --> 09:16:30.680
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Unprogrammed appropriations have been reduced approximately 112 billion or only 1.6% of the expenditure program.

asr-009920
09:16:30.680 --> 09:16:32.180
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: That is welcome.

asr-009921
09:16:33.240 --> 09:16:36.820
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: But transparency must also extend to program appropriations.

asr-009922
09:16:37.860 --> 09:16:48.180
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Congress should know, as far as practicable, the project, location, beneficiary, and purpose of the funds it appropriates.

asr-009923
09:16:48.660 --> 09:16:57.540
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Post-enactment discretion through lump sums, realignments, and release conditions should remain limited and transparent.

asr-009924
09:16:58.640 --> 09:17:09.220
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Kung ang kongreso ang may power of the purse dapat malinaw sa atin kung saan papunta ang pera sa oras na aprobahan natin ang budget.

asr-009925
09:17:10.020 --> 09:17:14.080
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: And accountability should continue after enactment.

asr-009926
09:17:14.400 --> 09:17:18.080
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Indeed, an appropriation is not an

asr-009927
09:17:18.220 --> 09:17:18.540
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: accomplishment.

asr-009928
09:17:19.480 --> 09:17:27.080
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: What matters is what kind is what was actually implemented and whether it improved people's lives.

asr-009929
09:17:28.140 --> 09:17:37.480
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Representative Robert Nazal of [unclear] also cautioned against unlawful or manufactured savings.

asr-009930
09:17:38.720 --> 09:17:42.780
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Unspent funds should not automatically become savings.

asr-009931
09:17:42.780 --> 09:17:46.320
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: And projects should not be delayed.

asr-009932
09:17:46.920 --> 09:17:47.980
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Merely to create funds

asr-009933
09:17:48.220 --> 09:17:50.880
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: for transfer elsewhere.

asr-009934
09:17:51.920 --> 09:18:01.060
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Every declaration of savings must have a clear legal basis, proper documentation, and accountability.

asr-009935
09:18:02.360 --> 09:18:16.120
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Relatedly, Representative Edgar Erice of the 2nd District of Caloocan raised an important constitutional concern regarding the local government support fund.

asr-009936
09:18:16.120 --> 09:18:18.120
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: and amount of discretion

asr-009937
09:18:18.220 --> 09:18:23.520
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: that may remain after Congress approves the budget.

asr-009938
09:18:23.520 --> 09:18:36.360
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: The Supreme Court has upheld the LGU as a valid appropriation where it has sufficiently defined purpose and adequate standards governing its implementation.

asr-009939
09:18:36.980 --> 09:18:39.680
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: But this concern deserves attention.

asr-009940
09:18:39.680 --> 09:18:46.680
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Kung pagkatapos nating aprobahan ng budget, saka pa lamang malalaman kung aling LGU ang makakakuha,

asr-009941
09:18:48.220 --> 09:18:50.780
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: magkano ang makakatanggap at kung anong proyekto ang pupunduhan,

asr-009942
09:18:51.780 --> 09:18:59.600
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Congress must carefully examine whether it has sufficiently exercised its own power of appropriation.

asr-009943
09:19:00.440 --> 09:19:05.440
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: The issue is not whether we should assist our LGUs.

asr-009944
09:19:06.000 --> 09:19:06.720
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: We should.

asr-009945
09:19:06.720 --> 09:19:13.520
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: The issue is whether the GAA itself provides clear and objective standards

asr-009946
09:19:13.520 --> 09:19:18.200
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: so that the allocation of billions of pesos in local government

asr-009947
09:19:18.220 --> 09:19:24.740
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: support remains consistent with Congress' constitutional power of the purse.

asr-009948
09:19:25.920 --> 09:19:26.720
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Madam Speaker,

asr-009949
09:19:27.980 --> 09:19:31.660
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: the minority recognizes the good provisions of this measure.

asr-009950
09:19:32.560 --> 09:19:35.640
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: We recognize the reduction of the unprogrammed operations.

asr-009951
09:19:36.640 --> 09:19:39.340
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: We recognize the need for fiscal discipline.

asr-009952
09:19:39.980 --> 09:19:46.360
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: We recognize the programs and infrastructure investments that can contribute to growth.

asr-009953
09:19:46.360 --> 09:19:47.620
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: And we appreciate

asr-009966
09:19:47.620 --> 09:19:56.600
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: the majority's willingness to subject this budget to sustained scrutiny, but our reservations remain.

asr-009967
09:19:58.160 --> 09:20:02.700
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: The fiscal choices before us are therefore difficult.

asr-009968
09:20:03.760 --> 09:20:11.480
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Economic growth has slowed, inflation continues to weigh most heavily on poorer households,

asr-009969
09:20:11.480 --> 09:20:21.140
