asr-010016
09:23:52.600 --> 09:23:59.060
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero, sabi ng ordinaryong Pilipino, di ko ramdam. Bakit ganon?

asr-010017
09:23:59.060 --> 09:24:06.740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: For decades, the national budget has faithfully supported one set of policies.

asr-010018
09:24:07.240 --> 09:24:15.620
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Often called neoliberal or free market policies. Ito po yung privatization, deregulation, and liberalization.

asr-010019
09:24:16.580 --> 09:24:27.160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Under these policies, the things a nation needs just to function are now owned by a handful of families and conglomerates.

asr-010020
09:24:27.160 --> 09:24:36.540
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Energy. Oil and gas. Electricity. Water. Telecommunications. Our expressways.

asr-010021
09:24:37.240 --> 09:24:48.300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Airports. Seaports. Dating nasa kamay ng gobyerno, ngayon, malalaking profit centers pinagkikitaan ng iilan.

asr-010022
